    {/* THE ADDRESS IS NOW A LINK, AND IT SHOULD ALWAYS HAVE BEEN ONE.
        This page's whole argument is that you do not have to trust it: every figure is an
        eth_call at a stated block, so go and check. Checking meant selecting a 42-character
        hex string, copying it by hand, and finding an explorer yourself. The site had exactly
        ZERO external links on any page — it named Hyperliquid, Binance, Bybit, Coinbase and
        these contracts and linked to none of them — so it participated in no link graph in
        either direction, and the checkability it is proudest of was gated behind clerical work.
        #readContract lands on the tab where the same getters this page calls can be called by
