          <p class="section-note">{fill(e.note ?? "", { supply: num(e.totalSupply), endYear: e.distributionEnd ? String(new Date(`${e.distributionEnd}T00:00:00Z`).getUTCFullYear()) : "" })}{p && (
            <>{" "}<code>dripRate()</code>{" "}returns {`${e.ratePerBlock} ${e.symbol}`} per block, about {num(e.perDay)} a day, and has done since block {e.startBlock.toLocaleString("en-US")}.
            By the stated block, {reg.verifiedBlock.toLocaleString("en-US")}, the contract&rsquo;s own arithmetic says {`${num(p.owed)} ${e.symbol}`} should
            have been dripped, and <code>dripped()</code>{" "}says {num(p.dripped)} actually was. The difference, {`${num(p.gap)} ${e.symbol}`} or {pct(p.gap / e.totalSupply)} of
            total supply, is what the contract owed on paper at that block, and every block since adds {`${e.ratePerBlock} ${e.symbol}`} more.{e.heldNow === 0 && " Its balance at that block was zero, so none of it could move."}</>
          )}</p>
          <p class="section-note"><strong>What this does not say:</strong>{" "}{e.caveat}{" "}{e.detail}</p>
        </>
        );
      })}
    </>
  )}

  <h2 class="section" id="releasing">{state("releasing").label}</h2>
